From c8310ae13a0e8832cd80cc8f01ce4f1e2afa0a2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skate3Recomp iOS port <lmccjake@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:22:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] thread: hand-written arm64 fiber switch for iOS

getcontext/makecontext/swapcontext are absent from the iOS SDK, and the fiber
primitive is not optional - guest thread scheduling in xthread.cpp and
kernel_state.cpp is built on it.

fiber_arm64_apple.S saves and restores the AAPCS64 callee-saved set (x19-x28,
x29, x30, d8-d15) in a 160-byte 16-byte-aligned frame. fiber_ios.cpp fabricates
one of those frames by hand when starting a fiber, with the link register slot
pointing at Trampoline and a null frame pointer so backtraces terminate at the
base of the fiber stack instead of running on into unrelated memory. Semantics
match the POSIX backend exactly, so nothing above this changes.

This is register movement, not code generation: no JIT entitlement, no W^X
concern. It targets arm64, not arm64e, so it does not sign return addresses.

fiber_posix.cpp now excludes iOS explicitly, since REX_PLATFORM_MAC is true
there as well.

Checked: assembles for arm64-apple-ios and disassembles to the intended frame
layout, with the offsets the C++ side assumes; fiber_ios.cpp compiles clean for
iOS and emits no symbols off it; fiber_posix.cpp still builds for macOS. The
switch has not been executed - see tests/ios in the game repo for a round-trip
test that runs natively on an Apple Silicon Mac.
